' diagram-type: state-machine
@startuml
title v0002 State Registry - Team-Scoped Task Lifecycle State Machine

state "created" as Created
state "dispatched" as Dispatched
state "running" as Running
state "finished" as Finished
state "failed" as Failed

[*] --> Created : Registry\nlistener identity authorized for task.team_id\nINSERT team-owned task + created(executor_id=NULL)\nin one transaction

Created --> Dispatched : Registry\natomic same-team + same-tag approval\nset immutable tasks.executor_id + approved_at\nINSERT dispatched(executor_id=NULL)

Dispatched --> Running : Assigned same-team Executor\nINSERT running with non-null executor_id\nenvelope team_id = authenticated Executor team\nnew (occurred_at,event_id) > latest

Running --> Finished : Assigned same-team Executor\nINSERT finished with strictly later tuple\nenvelope team_id = authenticated Executor team
Running --> Failed : Assigned same-team Executor\nINSERT failed with strictly later tuple\nenvelope team_id = authenticated Executor team

Finished --> [*]
Failed --> [*]

note right of Created
  Task team invariant:
    Every task has exactly one immutable team_id.
    Listener identity must be authorized for it.
    Dedupe key is
    (team_id, source, source_task_id).
    No discovery occurs before commit.
end note

note right of Dispatched
  Approval invariant:
    task.team_id = executor.team_id
    required_tag = registered single tag
    exactly one same-team winner
    foreign task_id -> unknown-shape 404
    later same-team winner -> 409
    tasks.executor_id never changes.
end note

note right of Running
  Executor-event invariant:
    caller is authenticated assigned Executor
    envelope team_id equals authenticated Executor team
    envelope executor_id is NOT NULL
    append and projection update share a transaction.
end note

note as Ownership
  Event ownership:
    Registry emits created and dispatched
      with task_events.executor_id = NULL
      and team_id inherited from the task row.
    Assigned same-team Executor emits
      running, finished, failed
      with executor_id = tasks.executor_id
      and envelope team_id equal to
      the authenticated Executor team
      (which State Registry verifies).
    Every child row inherits and enforces
      the task's immutable team ownership.
end note

note as Ordering
  Idempotency and strict ordering:
    Resolve identical (task_id,event_id) retry first.
    Every fresh lifecycle event must have
      (occurred_at,event_id) strictly greater
      than the latest accepted tuple.
    Read by occurred_at ASC, event_id ASC.
    Equal timestamps require a greater event_id.
    accepted_sequence and all recovery overrides
      are rejected and never affect ordering.
end note

note as Rejections
  Reject without append or projection change:
    - running before dispatched
    - finished or failed before running
    - any fresh event after terminal state
    - unassigned same-team Executor
    - envelope team_id != authenticated Executor team
    - foreign-team task or Executor (404 as unknown)
    - non-increasing ordering tuple
    - caller-supplied accepted_sequence.
end note

@enduml
